# **Experiment 1: Introduction to Network Simulator**

### **Aim**

To study the Network Simulator (NS2) and understand its basic features.

### **Simple code**

```
set ns [new Simulator]

set nf [open out.nam w]
$ns namtrace-all $nf

set n0 [$ns node]
set n1 [$ns node]

$ns duplex-link $n0 $n1 1Mb 10ms DropTail

set udp [new Agent/UDP]
$ns attach-agent $n0 $udp

set null [new Agent/Null]
$ns attach-agent $n1 $null

$ns connect $udp $null

set cbr [new Application/Traffic/CBR]
$cbr attach-agent $udp

$ns at 1.0 "$cbr start"
$ns at 4.0 "$cbr stop"

proc finish {} {
    global ns nf
    $ns flush-trace
    close $nf
    exec nam out.nam &
    exit 0
}

$ns at 5.0 "finish"
$ns run
```

### **Explanation**

- `Simulator`: Creates a new network simulator.
- `node`: Creates network devices.
- `duplex-link`: Connects two nodes.
- `UDP`: Provides transport communication.
- `CBR`: Generates constant bit-rate traffic.
- `namtrace-all`: Records network activity.
- `nam`: Displays the network animation.

