# **Experiment 10: Implementation of Wired and Wireless Ad-hoc Network using NS2**

### **Aim**

To simulate and implement wired and wireless ad-hoc networks using NS2.

### **Part A: Wired Network**

A wired network uses physical communication links such as cables to connect computers.

### **Simple code**

```
set ns [new Simulator]

set nf [open wired.nam w]
$ns namtrace-all $nf

set n0 [$ns node]
set n1 [$ns node]
set n2 [$ns node]

$ns duplex-link $n0 $n1 1Mb 10ms DropTail
$ns duplex-link $n1 $n2 1Mb 10ms DropTail

set udp [new Agent/UDP]
$ns attach-agent $n0 $udp

set null [new Agent/Null]
$ns attach-agent $n2 $null

$ns connect $udp $null

set cbr [new Application/Traffic/CBR]
$cbr attach-agent $udp

$ns at 1.0 "$cbr start"
$ns at 4.0 "$cbr stop"

proc finish {} {
    global ns nf
    $ns flush-trace
    close $nf
    exec nam wired.nam &
    exit 0
}

$ns at 5.0 "finish"
$ns run
```

### **Explanation**

- Three nodes are created.
- Nodes are connected using wired links.
- UDP sends packets.
- CBR generates traffic.
- NAM displays packet transmission.

